{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The memory card fits my repeated use of removable storage across devices; extra capacity could be useful if it is compatible, although I already own a reader.",
    "The powered USB hub could help connect the readers and cables I use, while a Fire TV Stick could add streaming to my existing TV setup if compatible."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo speakers and smart display introduce voice assistance that I have not been looking for; owning a Fire tablet does not mean I want those functions.",
    "The internal SSD does not serve the same need as removable memory cards, and a 24-port switch is far beyond my current connection needs."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire tablet purchase seems to have been taken as interest in more Amazon devices, even when they serve different purposes.",
    "My use of storage and connection accessories seems to have been stretched into interest in any storage or networking equipment, regardless of how I would use it."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I repeatedly choose accessories that support equipment I already use, so compatibility and a clear practical purpose matter more than simply being another electronic device.",
    "What I already own matters: another card reader needs a reason to be useful, and the three streaming sticks are alternatives from which I would choose just one."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my need for practical device accessories but stretched that interest into unrelated smart devices and larger upgrades."
}"}
